[128.478335, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_01TYWTW93sMYAtbaZx9bnXn1\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The program works. The output format looks correct. Let me verify the calculations. Looking at the second application:\\n- LOAN-AMOUNT: 5000 (0000005000)\\n- PROPERTY-VALUE: 4000 (0000004000)\\n- DOWN-PAYMENT: 3500 (0000003500)\\n- TERM: 01 (year)\\n- RATE: 00550 (5.50%)\\n\\nWait, the minimum down payment should be 15% of property value = 4000 * 0.15 = 600. The down payment is 3500, which is more than 600, so it should be approved. That's correct.\\n\\nBut looking at the first application:\\n- LOAN: 2000000000\\n- PROPERTY: 3500000000\\n- DOWN: 0500000000\\n- TERM: 20 years\\n- RATE: 5.50%\\n\\nMIN_DOWN = 3500000000 * 0.15 = 525000000. DOWN = 500000000, which is less than 525000000, so it should be denied. That's correct.\\n\\nHowever, I notice there's a spacing issue in the denied record - it says \\\"DENY \\\" with a space, but the expected output shows \\\"DEN"]
