[177.826448, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_01J54cXEx9FQbLLS8frSU31E\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The output format now matches the expected format. Let me verify the calculations for the approved application:\\n\\nApplication 2:\\n- LOAN_AMOUNT: 5000\\n- PROPERTY_VALUE: 4000\\n- DOWN_PAYMENT: 3500\\n- TERM: 1 year = 12 months\\n- RATE: 5.50%\\n\\nVerification:\\n- MIN_DOWN = 4000 * 0.15 = 600. DOWN_PAYMENT (3500) > MIN_DOWN (600) ✓ Approved\\n- MONTHLY_RATE = 5.50 / 1200 = 0.00458333...\\n- MONTHLY_PAYMENT = 5000 * 0.00458333 / (1 - (1 + 0.00458333)^(-12))\\n  = 22.9166... / (1 - 0.9465...)\\n  = 22.9166... / 0.0534...\\n  ≈ 429.01\\n\\nHmm, the calculations look off. Let me check the expected output in the example:\\n```\\n001 00000400.00 00000022.92 00000377.08 0000004622.92\\n```\\n\\nThis shows a monthly payment of ~400, not 2316. Let me recalculate:\\n\\nLooking at the example values:\\n- Payment: 400\\n- Interest: 22.92\\n- Principal: 377.08\\n- Balance"]
[177.826611, "o", " after 1st payment: 4622.92\\n\\nIf balance after payment is 4622.92, and principal was 377.08, then starting loan was about 5000. \\nInterest of 22.92 on 5000 = 22.92/5000 = 0.4584% monthly rate = 5.5% annual.\\n\\nWait, I see the issue. Looking at my input:\\n- LOAN-AMOUNT: 0000005000 = 5000\\n- But my WS-RATE PIC is 9(3)V9(2), and the input is \\\"00550\\\"\\n\\nSo the rate should be parsed as 005.50 = 5.50%. That seems correct.\\n\\nLet me trace through the calculation more carefully. The monthly payment I'm getting is 2316.70, which is way too high.\\n\\nWait! I see the problem. Looking at the interest calculation: 2291.67 is the interest part. That's 5000 * 0.458333 = 2291.67. So my monthly rate is being calculated as 0.458333 instead of 0.00458333!\\n\\nThe issue is the division by 1200. Let me check: 550 / 1200 = 0.458333. But my rate is stored as 005.50 (5.50), so 5.50 / 1200 = 0.00458333.\\n\\nWait, looking at the input again: \\\"00550\\\". With PIC 9(3)V9(2), this should be interpreted as 005.50 = 5.50.\\n\\nLet me check wh"]
[177.826631, "o", "at's happening:\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":568,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":32186,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":568,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3a874076-d366-42a6-b946-23aabe6d27d3\",\"uuid\":\"1854ab79-3e1c-4a30-bf4b-8e9a765eac62\"}\r\n"]
[182.267505, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_01J54cXEx9FQbLLS8frSU31E\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_0154W4ZYBzBjkfUb23fX1Jwu\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cat > /tmp/test.cbl << 'EOF'\\n       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.\\n       PROGRAM-ID. TEST-RATE.\\n       DATA DIVISION.\\n       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.\\n       01 WS-RATE         PIC 9(3)V9(2).\\n       01 WS-RATE-DISP    PIC 9(3).9(2).\\n       01 WS-MONTHLY-RATE PIC 9V9(10).\\n       PROCEDURE DIVISION.\\n           MOVE \\\"00550\\\" TO WS-RATE.\\n           MOVE WS-RATE TO WS-RATE-DISP.\\n           DISPLAY \\\"RATE: \\\" WS-RATE-DISP.\\n           COMPUTE WS-MONTHLY-RATE = WS-RATE / 1200.\\n           DISPLAY \\\"MONTHLY RATE: \\\" WS-MONTHLY-RATE.\\n           STOP RUN.\\nEOF\\ncobc -x -fixed /tmp/test.cbl -o /tmp/test && /tmp/test\",\"description\":\"Test rate parsing\"}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":568,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":"]
