[183.064585, "o", "{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_0154W4ZYBzBjkfUb23fX1Jwu\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"RATE: 550.00\\nMONTHLY RATE: 0.4583333333\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3a874076-d366-42a6-b946-23aabe6d27d3\",\"uuid\":\"c8a51d95-7cf1-4e4e-b0ef-ead3b7169447\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"RATE: 550.00\\nMONTHLY RATE: 0.4583333333\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false}}\r\n"]
[194.278342, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_016ziKbiYnTduy9SpA8MbBxo\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I see the problem. The input \\\"00550\\\" is being interpreted as 550.00 instead of 005.50. The issue is that when moving a string \\\"00550\\\" to a PIC 9(3)V9(2), COBOL treats the value numerically and the string becomes 550 with no implied decimal.\\n\\nLooking at the input format:\\n- Input: `00550` for RATE\\n- Expected interpretation: 5.50% (which would be 005.50 in PIC 9(3)V9(2) format)\\n\\nThe issue is that when using string-to-numeric conversion, COBOL doesn't automatically insert the implied decimal. I need to handle this differently.\\n\\nLet me check the input data format again:\\n- RATE - 9(3)V9(2) - this means 3 integer digits and 2 decimal digits\\n\\nLooking at the example output which shows payment of ~400 for 5000 loan at rate resulting in ~23 interest:\\n- 23 = 5000 * (rate/12) → rate = 23*12/5000 = 0.0552 = 5.52%\\n\\nSo the rate 00550 sh"]
[194.278391, "o", "ould be interpreted as 5.50%. The format is 9(3)V9(2), meaning the last 2 digits are decimal. So \\\"00550\\\" = 005.50 = 5.50.\\n\\nThe problem is how COBOL parses a text string into a numeric with implied decimal. I need to use REDEFINES or move the characters appropriately.\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1075,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":32754,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":1075,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"3a874076-d366-42a6-b946-23aabe6d27d3\",\"uuid\":\"00a99b67-3acf-427b-9c47-9a1bb82702d3\"}\r\n"]
