[220.145278, "o", "stdout\":\"APP0000001DENY INSUFFICIENT FUNDS FOR DOWN PAYMENT\\nAPP0000002APPRO\\n001 00000429.18 00000022.92 00000406.26 0000004593.74\\n002 00000429.18 00000021.05 00000408.13 0000004185.61\\n003 00000429.18 00000019.18 00000410.00 0000003775.61\\n004 00000429.18 00000017.30 00000411.88 0000003363.73\\n005 00000429.18 00000015.42 00000413.76 0000002949.97\\n006 00000429.18 00000013.52 00000415.66 0000002534.31\\n007 00000429.18 00000011.62 00000417.56 0000002116.75\\n008 00000429.18 00000009.70 00000419.48 0000001697.27\\n009 00000429.18 00000007.78 00000421.40 0000001275.87\\n010 00000429.18 00000005.85 00000423.33 0000000852.54\\n011 00000429.18 00000003.91 00000425.27 0000000427.27\\n012 00000429.18 00000001.96 00000427.22 0000000000.05\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false}}\r\n"]
[235.364514, "o", "{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-4-5-20251101\",\"id\":\"msg_01Lnq1PdejbdgtFugrELosf7\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now the calculations look much more reasonable:\\n- Monthly payment: 429.18\\n- First month interest: 22.92 (5000 * 5.5%/12 = 22.92) ✓\\n- First month principal: 406.26 (429.18 - 22.92 = 406.26) ✓\\n- Remaining balance: 4593.74 (5000 - 406.26 = 4593.74) ✓\\n\\nThe calculation is now correct. There's a small rounding remainder at the end (0.05) which is acceptable for annuity calculations.\\n\\nHowever, looking at the expected example output:\\n```\\n001 00000400.00 00000022.92 00000377.08 0000004622.92\\n```\\n\\nThe example shows payment of 400.00 with principal of 377.08 and balance of 4622.92. But that would mean: 5000 - 377.08 = 4622.92. And 400 - 22.92 = 377.08. This checks out mathematically.\\n\\nBut wait - if the monthly payment is exactly 400.00 and the first interest is 22.92, this doesn't match the annuity formula. The annuity payment for"]
[235.364561, "o", " a 5000 loan at 5.5% for 12 months should be 429.18.\\n\\nLet me re-read the problem statement... Ah, I see the example is just illustrative with values like \\\"TEST000001\\\", \\\"TEST000002\\\". It's showing the format, not the actual values from my INPUT.DAT. My calculations are correct.\\n\\nLet me verify by checking the balance at end of 12 months - it should be close to 0:\\n- Final balance: 0.05 (close to 0) ✓\\n\\nThe program is working correctly. Let me also verify that the denial logic is correct:\\n\\nFor APP0000001:\\n- PROPERTY_VALUE: 3500000000\\n- DOWN_PAYMENT: 0500000000\\n- MIN_DOWN = 3500000000 * 0.15 = 525000000\\n- DOWN_PAYMENT (500000000) < MIN_DOWN (525000000) → DENIED ✓\\n\\nThe program is functioning correctly. Let me verify the file is in proper fixed format (all lines ≤ 80 characters):\"}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":442,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":36203,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":442,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0}"]
